    "result_text": "All 45 tests pass, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `checkDigit` field to the owner response \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` property to the owner schema (integer 0\u20139, read-only), placed after `customerCode`. `OwnerDto` is code-generated from this spec, so this creates the field on the DTO.\n\n2. **`mapper/CheckDigits.java`** (new) \u2014 a plain static helper computing the Luhn check digit over the digits in a string (non-digits ignored, null-safe). Kept as a standalone helper so MapStruct doesn't mistake it for an implicit mapping method, matching the existing `Localities` pattern.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` that populates `checkDigit` via `CheckDigits.luhn(owner.getCustomerCode())`, alongside the other derived-field mappings.\n\nThe Luhn implementation mirrors the algorithm the acceptance test replicates. `Cp31Tests` passes, and the full suite (45 tests) is green.",
